     "name": "What is the real performance difference between GaN and silicon chargers?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "GaN semiconductors have a 3.4 eV bandgap vs 1.1 eV for silicon, enabling 3 key advantages: (1) 93-95% efficiency vs 80-85% for silicon, meaning less energy wasted as heat; (2) 40-50% smaller volume at equivalent wattage because GaN needs smaller heat sinks; (3) 30% cooler operation, GaN V stabilizes at 58.3°C under 100% load vs 82.7°C for silicon at 25°C ambient. GaN supports up to 240W in compact form factors; silicon practically tops out around 100W. For B2B OEM buyers, this translates to lower return rates (2-5% vs 8-15% for silicon), 5+ year lifespan vs 2-3 years, and 40-60% higher retail margins on a 15-25% BOM premium."
     }
