 <p class="text-lg text-slate-700 italic"><strong>GaN chargers now account for over 50% of units above 65W</strong>, with GaN power IC costs dropping 8-12% annually. GaN achieves <strong>95%+ efficiency vs 85% for silicon</strong>, runs 30% cooler, and fits 240W into a 65W-sized enclosure. The <a href="https://commission.europa.eu/energy-climate-change-environment/standards-tools-and-labels/products-labelling-rules-and-requirements/sustainable-products/ecodesign-sustainable-products-regulation_en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brandBlue hover:underline">EU Ecodesign Regulation (ESPR)</a> and <a href="https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dir/2022/2380/oj" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brandBlue hover:underline">Common Charger Directive</a> have made GaN the compliance path for chargers above 45W. This comparison covers the OEM metrics that determine your BOM: efficiency at full load, case temperature under sustained operation, cost by wattage tier, and field return rate data.</p>
